<title>SPAIN: BT to exit Airtel, MCI has TISA option-CNMV.</title>
<headline>BT to exit Airtel, MCI has TISA option-CNMV.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>An alliance between Telefonica de Espana, U.S.-based MCI and British Telecom includes a committment from BT to exit Airtel, according to a statement on the deal issued on Friday by Spain's Stock Market Commission CNMV.</p>
<p>The deal also gives MCI the option to purchase up to 10 percent of Telefonica's International arm, TISA, if Telefonica were to put up some of its 76.3 percent TISA stake. The remaining Spanish state stake in TISA is excluded from this deal, the Telefonica statement to the CNMV said.</p>
</text>
